Subject: [PATCH] dma-heap: a52sxq: register qcom,secure-bitstream (VMID_CP_BITSTREAM)

Applied 2026-11-24 to soc-repo + soc-repo-staging (SPEC 04 gap vid.dec.secure; proposed 11-23). Built out of tree: drivers612/secure/secheap/build.sh.
Applies to bsp612/soc-repo (patch -p1).

drivers612/gpu-video/video/msm/vidc/msm_smem.c (secure_heap_for_buffer_type) asks
for the dma heap "qcom,secure-bitstream" for the secure decoder's input/scratch/persist
buffers and the secure encoder's output. The 6.12 heap driver only creates
qcom,secure-pixel and qcom,secure-non-pixel; the live heap list of the shipped kernel
(logs/selftest/PHONE1-20261122-193951 row quirk.dma_heaps) has no bitstream heap.
qcom_secure_system_heap_create() already handles QCOM_DMA_HEAP_FLAG_CP_BITSTREAM
(get_secure_vmid -> VMID_CP_BITSTREAM 0x9), so one more call is all it takes.

Test order (never first on a daily phone: on 2026-11-12 a secure ION allocation reset
the phone silently, and no later entry records that as fixed):
 1. kexec session on a test phone: /dev/dma_heap/qcom,secure-bitstream exists; allocate
    1 MiB from it and free it -> no reset, no hyp_assign error.
 2. Android: a secure decoder session (c2.qti.avc.decoder.secure configure + start)
    -> no "secure-bitstream" error line in dmesg.
 3. Hands: a Widevine L1 title plays in HD.
Module affected: qcom_dma_heaps.ko only (no export changes).

--- a/drivers/dma-buf/heaps/qcom_dma_heap.c	2026-11-23 18:41:53.235382088 +0200
+++ b/drivers/dma-buf/heaps/qcom_dma_heap.c	2026-11-23 18:41:53.235414108 +0200
@@ -45,6 +45,17 @@
 				       QCOM_DMA_HEAP_FLAG_CP_PIXEL);
 		qcom_secure_system_heap_create("qcom,secure-non-pixel", NULL,
 				       QCOM_DMA_HEAP_FLAG_CP_NON_PIXEL);
+		/*
+		 * a52sxq: the 5.4-era msm_vidc port takes the secure decoder's input,
+		 * scratch and persist buffers (and the secure encoder's output) from
+		 * this heap: VMID_CP_BITSTREAM, the venus_sec_bitstream context bank.
+		 * 5.4 served them from the ION secure system heap with
+		 * ION_FLAG_CP_BITSTREAM. Without the heap every secure session
+		 * (Widevine L1 playback, HDCP wireless display) fails at its first
+		 * internal buffer.
+		 */
+		qcom_secure_system_heap_create("qcom,secure-bitstream", NULL,
+				       QCOM_DMA_HEAP_FLAG_CP_BITSTREAM);
 	}
 	qcom_sys_movable_heap_create();
 
